<title>USA: U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA wheat export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net sales reductions of 66,700 metric tons (MT)--a marketing-year low--were primarily the result of increases for the Philippines (26,100 MT) being more than offset by reductions for unknown destinations (77,300 MT), Trinidad (21,000 MT), and Mexico (12,600 MT).</p>
<p>Exports of 246,800 MT were up one-third from the week earlier, but down one-quarter from the 4-week average.  The primary destinations were Turkey (67,300 MT), Japan (41,300 MT), Taiwan (35,700 MT), and Mexico (30,200 MT).</p>
</text>
